From: =?UTF-8?q?Torbj=C3=B8rn=20Ludvigsen?= <tobben@fastmail.fm>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:26:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Correct open-loop cable torque balance without destabilizing
 damping changes

Adapt the physical-inertia correction from PR #77. Electromagnetic torque
already accelerates the rotor; adding holding stiffness only to cable response
artificially boosts coarse-step holding strength. Mirror the correction in
JS, Rust/native/Wasm and Python/Warp preparation, preserving closed-loop
constraint stiffness and reserving the retired ABI option slot.

Add independent spring-loaded-spool equilibrium tests across timesteps and
backends, update old stiffness expectations, and wire the regression into CI.
Document matched Squares replays and why the separate damping correction is
deferred: both the full PR physics patch and damping-only variant fail the
unchanged one-substep loaded-state gate.

Validation: npm run test:physics (11 passed); analytic JS/Rust (20 passed);
Python/Warp (117 passed, 5 skipped); native/Wasm/mounted/substeps (141 passed,
1 skipped); full Jest (801 passed, 1 skipped). Squares remains timestep
sensitive; no hardware or complete-print accuracy claim.
